id: pm-rl-lifecycle
title: Migrate evaluation lifecycle APIs to a clock-independent ordering contract
description: "Follow-up to pm-rl-sequential. Migrate the evaluation lifecycle to review approved -> Plan sealed -> all collection Runs -> candidate -> ordered checkpoints/looks -> promotion, with a clock-independent proof of artifact ordering. The accepted chronology guards and creation-order regression proofs in PR107 complete the current sequential-evaluation scope; this migration is separate work."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: api,evaluation-lifecycle,"gh:unbraind/pm-rl#153"
created_at: "2026-10-27T05:03:56.149Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-11T17:45:46.439Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Migrate the typed SDK and CLI to one lifecycle contract: review approved -> Plan sealed -> all collection Runs -> candidate -> ordered checkpoints/looks -> promotion; document the migration and preserve fixed-sample behavior.; Prove lifecycle ordering independently of wall-clock timestamps, including clock skew, equal timestamps and rollback; every promotion and approval path calls the same validator and adversarial artifact-pair permutations refuse every out-of-order transition."
comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T05:56:09.951Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 correction to the previous scope split: PR 107 now requires complete chronology coverage for all existing artifacts, including every collection Run before the candidate and every cumulative look. That correctness fix stays in pm-rl-sequential. This Feature still exclusively tracks the public lifecycle API migration and clock-independent ordering proof; it does not block that fix or expand its API."
  "2026-10-31T15:36:42.952Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yR9cm: corrected description and acceptance_criteria with pm update to review approved -> Plan sealed -> all collection Runs -> candidate -> ordered checkpoints/looks -> promotion. Verified against reviewSequentialPlan, evaluationLifecycleArtifacts and README. Clock-independent ordering and fixed-sample compatibility requirements remain. This corrects planning text only; the future API migration remains open."
  "2026-11-06T20:18:52.587Z",codex-astra,"Orientation complete. The item has no parent; read its originating sequential feature and the package architecture and README. The current lifecycle uses creation timestamps and timestamp-sorted SDK mutation events, so event-list positions are not an independent ordering proof. Investigating a versioned durable causal receipt while preserving existing fixed-plan serialization and readers."
  "2026-11-06T20:26:14.871Z",codex-astra,"Implementation uses explicit ordering=causal/1 on new sequential plans. SDK-created birth witnesses bind the exact comparison, stage, random nonce and certified predecessor births in the same native create as the artifact. Existing plans retain their original timestamp contract and hashes. Added an attributable design-approval API/command and collection admission through run start; candidate, look and promotion readers share causal validation. Testing equal clocks, skew, rollback, cross-process contention and killed-writer replay without SDK mocks."
  "2026-11-06T20:39:09.673Z",codex-astra,"The first real-SDK skew/equal-clock and native process replay probes passed. The expanded suite exposed bounded lock contention, so process consumers now exercise bounded retry of the documented lock_conflict outcome. Causal validation now drains SDK reads before returning a refusal. Public main replay used 64 records in one repository unit, clocks decreasing from 2032 to 2028, unchanged authoritative source digest, descriptive mean 0.734375 versus 0.5 and exhausted/refused statistics. Legacy behavior remains unchanged; no policy-improvement claim."
  "2026-11-06T20:48:41.928Z",codex-astra,"The clock-order function-only revert fails the real SDK skew regression; restoring it passes. Public creation witnesses are also included in decision seals, so a changed retained witness refuses promotion retry through the established card_drift wrapper. The native SDK snapshot test runner supports pm_context=none only with an isolated or snapshot workspace; using snapshot for the linked gate. No SDK mocks or dependency changes."
  "2026-11-06T21:00:17.252Z",codex-astra,"Verification complete: the linked real-SDK snapshot gate passes 5/5 tests with 100% lines, branches and functions for evaluation-lifecycle.ts. Three isolated function-only reverts each fail one regression and each restoration passes: timestamp dispatch, causal precedence and existing-birth reuse. Five legacy checks pass, including 500 published-schema cases, released native fixtures, 460200 chronology permutations, full history pagination and fixed results. Typecheck, build, test compilation, lint, 539 declaration docstrings and zero duplication pass. Public source evidence and revert receipts are linked. Full npm/Bun release gates remain assigned to PR CI at unchanged thresholds; no SDK bug established. The complete opt-in lifecycle migration is implemented, with legacy plans preserved and the native-history trust boundary documented."
  "2026-11-06T21:03:29.410Z",codex-astra,"Self-review found that causal Run retries must preserve the existing configuration-hash invariant as well as body and environment identity. Adding fixed_version to the sealed birth projection and immutable retry envelope, with a real SDK mutation refusal and function-only revert proof. The first PR head is published and bot review is queued; final evidence will cover the correction."
  "2026-11-06T21:22:35.109Z",codex-astra,"Final correction verified: causal Run retries now seal and compare fixed_version, preserving the stored configuration-hash invariant. The real SDK drift test refuses without appending history. All 6 lifecycle tests pass in the linked snapshot gate with 100% lines, branches and functions for the new module. The complete isolated revert runner passes all 4 failure/restoration pairs, including configuration-hash checking; the public 64-record replay passes unchanged. Typecheck, build, test compilation, lint, docstrings and duplication checks pass. Investigation of identity aliases confirmed the existing comparison parser already refuses normalized collisions, so no redundant validator was added. PR 153 is open; CI and the explicitly queued review remain pending."
  "2026-11-06T21:33:40.508Z",codex-astra,"Review round 1: Greptile identified a valid existing-candidate retry bypass. The generic identical-record shortcut returns before the causal birth envelope check, allowing native fixed_version drift. Adding the same birth verification to existing candidate registration and preflight while preserving legitimate promotion bookkeeping, with a real SDK regression and a function-only revert proof. CodeQL passes the reviewed head; release CI and queued CodeRabbit remain pending."
  "2026-11-06T21:49:50.342Z",codex-astra,"Review round 1 fix verified for thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs60s2yE: existing causal candidates now share birth-envelope verification across registration and preflight before policy-card publication. Changed checkpoint metadata refuses without writes; retries after real promotion remain valid. The linked snapshot suite passes 7/7 with 100% lines, branches and functions for evaluation-lifecycle.ts. All seven lifecycle tests now have recorded function-only failure/restoration pairs, run as a five-case batch plus the schema and CLI selectors. Typecheck, build, test compilation, lint, docstrings and duplication checks pass. The restored passing cases include native process contention and killed acknowledgements. No SDK bug was established. Release CI and current-head external re-review remain pending; the item stays open for the orchestrator."
  "2026-11-09T09:54:27.899Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched all review threads and all comments with complete pagination. Three unresolved CodeRabbit threads concern proof failure-cause validation, measured runner counts, and repeated birth hashing. Latest review contains no Outside diff range findings. Merged current main, retaining the lifecycle approval command and current manifest version. Plan: structured runner evidence, refusal of infrastructure failures, per-validation digest cache, regression tests and isolated behavioral reverts. Full npm/Bun release gates are delegated to CI per the explicit slow-repository instruction; local targeted and quality gates retain all thresholds."
  "2026-11-09T10:03:46.579Z",codex-agent,"Self-review found an additional evidence flaw: workspace-recipe clocks did not consistently reach the SDK core entry point because the pinned SDK exposes separately bundled contexts. The strict proof checker rejected the old clock proof because it observed loop_write_conflict instead of an ordering refusal. Replaced fixture clock control with the Node process Date test clock, added native birth-timestamp assertions, and retained the complete real tracker flows. This changes test instrumentation only; SDK behavior is not mocked. No dependency bump or upstream issue was filed. Clean-home strict tracker health passes all gate-failing checks; default-home health sees a global pm-github host-version skew unrelated to this branch. Targeted repository checks passed 102/102 before this instrumentation improvement; final validation will rerun the affected tests."
  "2026-11-09T10:08:21.225Z",codex-agent,"Verified all ten isolated function-only revert cases with node test/evaluation-lifecycle.revert.ts: every mutation produced exactly 0 pass / 1 fail with the expected selected-test code and diagnostic, and every restoration produced 1 pass / 0 fail. PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs60v10P maps to validateProofRun failure admission, where removing infrastructure-failure exclusion makes proof rejects worker timeouts fail with Missing expected exception. PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs60v10c maps to validateProofRun measured counts, where restoring fixed counts makes proof records measured counts fail. PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs60v10V maps to validateCausalEvaluationOrder, where removing its shared digest cache makes hashes each birth fail. The clock dispatch association now observes eval_plan_late directly, rather than a later loop_write_conflict. docs/evaluation-lifecycle-revert.json retains all seven prior associations plus the three review regressions. Public tracker replay passes on 64 unchanged source records and now records/asserts all five native birth timestamps. SDK clock-context follow-up is pm-rl-sdk-clock-context."
  "2026-11-09T10:11:49.732Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted gate passes 102/102 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, with two workers, isolated Git identity and credentials excluded from child processes. Command is linked on this item. evaluation-lifecycle.ts remains 100% lines/branches/functions; whole-source statement coverage is left to unchanged CI gates. node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/evaluation-lifecycle-proof.test.ts also passes 4/4 through pm test --run --progress. Typecheck, build:test, build, lint, docstrings (539 declarations), duplication (zero clones), publication attestation (one attested publish), identity audit (five approved addresses), and production audit (zero vulnerabilities) pass. Ignored dist output was rebuilt; no dist files are tracked. All ten revert/restoration pairs and the 64-record public replay pass. No host-load timeout was accepted as proof. Full npm and Bun release gates are intentionally delegated to CI for this slow repository; no local full-gate certification is claimed. Strict health passes with an isolated home, while default-home health has a pre-existing global extension version skew. Remaining risk: final-head release CI and external re-review are pending. No threads were answered, resolved or reacted to, and no PR merge or release was performed."
  "2026-11-09T16:29:41.641Z",codex-agent,"Continuation inspection: retained remote head 90c58e6 and existing PR153/item; origin/main is already merged and the worktree is clean. Rule classes: behavioral evidence must identify the actual expected test failure, never process status alone; validated authoritative birth records must be reused throughout a causal operation. Audit all proof producers and causal creation/retry/read paths, including shared SDK/CLI output and packed consumers, then add adversarial regressions and isolated revert receipts. No new PR or duplicate item."
  "2026-11-09T16:36:43.038Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: evaluation-plan registration, collection start, candidate registration/preflight, sequential look creation/resume and manual/controller promotion share evaluation-lifecycle.ts. Creation now reuses validated predecessor births and digest cache; existing retries validate once and reuse the target birth. Exported validation remains Promise<void>; independent operations reread current witnesses. Six-stage real-SDK observation checks every birth/current pair for creation, validation and replay, including fresh drift refusal; no SDK result is substituted. All five revert generators now use shared selected-test TAP admission plus finally restoration, replacing status/global-AssertionError matching and assumed counts. Producer enumeration and adversarial worker-timeout tests enforce that rule package-wide. Packed npm and Bun consumers each passed full causal progression/retries, CLI JSON/TOON reads and changed-witness refusal on non-git trackers; tested artifact SHA256 19c7d17e8ff6636073c849dc1b4ae0fdd45f095c977c9645f5b99c57ca402442. Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Full npm/Bun release gates remain assigned to CI under the explicit slow-pm-rl exception; unchanged targeted and quality gates run locally."
  "2026-11-09T16:40:32.720Z",codex-agent,"Validation update: lifecycle/proof suite passed 14/14 with 100% lifecycle lines/branches/functions; proof-only pm test --run --progress passed 5/5. Both packed consumers passed. Historical proof execution correctly refused stale no-op selectors and unexpected assertion categories rather than publishing them. Updated selectors to current mutation/reader functions; strengthened reversed-history coverage to reorder actual SDK histories for scoped recovery clients too. The strengthened policy-card regression passes. No existing tests were deleted or weakened, and no infrastructure failure has been accepted as behavioral evidence. Strict health passes with isolated identity and existing advisories; production audit has zero vulnerabilities. Final receipt regeneration and compatibility/quality checks remain in progress."
  "2026-11-09T16:49:34.455Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof verified: all 42 behavioral mutation/restoration pairs pass: lifecycle 14, influence 10, compensation 3, executor 6, staging 4 and maintenance 5. PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs60v10P is covered by actual diagnostic/code admission, timeout exclusion, measured totals, all-five-producer enforcement and guaranteed source restoration; reverting those guards fails the linked adversarial proof tests. PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs61P8CY is covered by creation and retry mutants: duplicate validated-birth reads each cause Every native birth must be read once per causal operation, restoration passes. Final isolated-identity targeted command passes 104/104, zero failures/skips/cancellations, lifecycle 100% lines/branches/functions. Focused reversed-history test also passes and detects both attribution and snapshot-order mutants. Two historical receipt unchanged flags observed concurrent evidence/tracker updates; retain those observations in the implementation commit, then regenerate compensation and maintenance sequentially with a stable worktree. No timeout was accepted as proof."
  "2026-11-09T16:52:16.926Z",codex-agent,"Final verification for implementation aa5e6ef: sequential compensation and maintenance reruns both pass with measured reviewed_source_unchanged=true; all historical generators retain their observed failure diagnostics and measured counts. All 42 pairs pass with restored implementations. Targeted isolated-identity suite: 104/104, no failures/skips/cancellations, lifecycle 100% lines/branches/functions; focused history regression passes, proof-only pm test --run --progress 5/5. Typecheck, build:test, build, lint, docstrings (539 declarations), zero-clone duplication, publish attestation, approved identity audit, zero-vulnerability production audit and strict tracker health pass. Both captured npm/Bun consumer flows passed on non-git trackers. Native history remains a prefix-extension of origin/main; branch commits use only the required identity. Under-lease revalidation after discovery intentionally remains, while redundant birth reads inside one operation are removed. Full npm and Bun release gates remain pending for the pushed head in CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/workflows/ci.yml . No release or merge; review threads remain untouched for orchestrator/bot verification. Claim released with the item left in progress."
  "2026-11-11T17:28:06.589Z",codex-smallfix3-1111,"Read seven review threads and all comments; two unresolved findings. Inspected the 34-file saved WIP against base 70c39db. Select only the failure-cause admission change and its regression; implement locale-independent replay ordering locally without the unrelated JSON identity migration. Scoped tests, lint and typecheck will retain existing thresholds."
  "2026-11-11T17:31:57.339Z",codex-smallfix3-1111,"Regression suite passes 7/7 with zero skipped. Disposable reverts independently restoring localeCompare in traversal and in member selection each fail the code-point assertion (exit 1); restoring only the old causal-proof admission fails the legitimate timeout-word control (exit 1). Fixed rerun passes 7/7; lint, typecheck and build:test pass. Selected only the saved causal-proof change and its proof test. Left out all saved production-module JSON identity/order migration, other acceptance scripts, unrelated tests and prior PM changes; replay ordering is scoped to the acceptance helper."
  "2026-11-11T17:41:32.587Z",codex-smallfix3-1111,Importer verification found the lifecycle revert producer still targeted the old broad admission regex. Updated that producer to revert the scoped failure-cause check; this is required companion maintenance for the reviewed fixture change. Other saved WIP remains excluded. Running the affected producer selectors and remaining direct consumers in a disposable checkout.
  "2026-11-11T17:45:44.603Z",codex-smallfix3-1111,"Read the new PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs62Sa5Z finding in full: the observed stale mutation selector is fixed. Original selector fails at source.includes; six updated lifecycle producer cases now each record behavioral failure on revert and passing restoration. The other eight unchanged lifecycle cases had already passed their proof pairs. All four other direct proof producers pass: training influence 8 pairs, compensation 3, maintenance 5, executor 6. Public replay acceptance also passes using the actual public commit and public tracker copy. Final focused suite passes 7/7, lint, typecheck and build:test pass. All temporary receipt outputs stay outside tracked files."
  "2026-11-11T17:45:45.544Z",codex-smallfix3-1111,"Saved WIP exclusions (30 files): existing PM feature/history records; dataset.ts, improver-data.ts, improver-environment.ts, improver.ts, index.ts, invalidate.ts, json-identity.ts, meta.ts, policy-card.ts, state-boundary.ts, tracker-record.ts, scripts/live-baseline.ts; test/evaluation-plan.acceptance.ts, test/fixtures/boundary-classes.ts, test/fixtures/main-controller-compatibility.ts, test/fixtures/proposer-public.ts, test/index.test.ts, test/meta.test.ts, test/mutation-preflight.test.ts, test/policy-card.acceptance.ts, test/policy-card.test.ts, test/process.test.ts, test/sdk-adoption-differential.ts, test/sequential-evaluation.acceptance.ts, test/sequential-evaluation.test.ts, test/shadow.acceptance.ts, test/training-influence.acceptance.ts, test/worst-cohort.acceptance.ts. Selected only proof admission, proof tests, replay ordering and the corresponding producer selector; no production migration or historical PM rewrite. Saved local WIP branch removed after the first successful push."
